      "message": "I would propose a more telling name: something like `assert_before_after_eq!`. I would have expected `desugured!` to take and desugar a single input.\n\nActually, perhaps you can make this easier to use in tests by creating a function (you know, they still exist 😄) which takes a string as input and gives you back the analyzer output.\n\nThen the tests would look something like this\n\n```\nassert_eq!(\n    desugar(\"blah blah\"),\n    degugar(\"more blah\"),\n);       \n```",
