      "side": 1,
      "message": "I recently saw a trick to ensure that this code stays up to date: use exhausting unpacking to ensure you mention all fields:\n\n```\nlet Tag { id: self_id, value: self_value, loc: _ } \u003d self;\nlet Tag { id: other_id, value: other_value, loc: _ } \u003d other;\nself_id \u003d\u003d self_other \u0026\u0026 self_value \u003d\u003d other_value\n```\n\nIt\u0027s a bit verbose, but also kind of neat. You could implement this if you like.",
